It's not too cheerful news for the Java supporters
here that both the Java projects are defunct. The
other three at least don't say they are defunct, and
the one in C is the most advanced.

I have to have a warm spot in my heart for the fifth
project. The conventional wisdom in the software
maintenance/upgrade community is to rewrite the
software for maintainability _before_ doing any
large scale bug fixing or enhancements, and this
seems to be their project direction in project 5.

